Open/closed principle (OCP)
The open/closed principle, the O in SOLID, is represented by the different
InventoryCommand classes. Instead of having an implementation of the
InventoryCommand class per command, the team could have defined a single class
containing multiple if statements. Each if statement would determine what functionality
to execute. For example, the following illustrates how the team could have broken this
principle:
